: "N.common", "y": "T"}], "lens": [{"a": 29, "b": 29, "l": "kt", "alt": ["worry"], "o": "To panic is to suddenly feel so afraid that you cannot think clearly."}, {"a": 30, "b": 30, "l": "pw", "alt": ["Rather"], "o": "Instead shows that we do one thing in place of another (not panicking → looking for clues)."}, {"a": 43, "b": 43, "l": "kt", "alt": ["signs", "clues"], "o": "Hints are small pieces of help that point you towards an answer."}, {"a": 47, "b": 47, "l": "kt", "alt": ["figure out", "guess", "infer"], "o": "To work out something is to find the answer by thinking about it."}, {"a": 55, "b": 55, "l": "kt", "alt": [], "o": "A definition tells you exactly what a word means, like the drought example."}, {"a": 63, "b": 63, "l": "kt", "alt": ["directly"], "o": "Immediately = straight after, with nothing in between."}, {"a": 81, "b": 81, "l": "kt", "alt": [], "o": "A synonym is a word with the same or a very similar meaning (famished = very hungry). Antonyms are opposites."}, {"a": 88, "b": 88, "l": "pw", "alt": ["since", "as"], "o": "Because gives the reason: it works the same way for this reason."}, {"a": 97, "b": 97, "l": "kt", "alt": ["common"], "o": "Familiar = known to you. The writer adds an easier word you already know."}, {"a": 124, "b": 124, "l": "kt", "alt": [], "o": "Opposite = as different as possible (hot / cold). Unlike, but and while signal a contrast."}, {"a": 156, "b": 156, "l": "kt", "alt": ["guess", "work out", "tell"], "o": "A reader infers a meaning from clues. Careful: a writer implies, a reader infers."}, {"a": 168, "b": 168, "l": "kt", "alt": ["shows"], "o": "Suggests = points towards something without saying it directly."}, {"a": 181, "b": 181, "l": "pw", "alt": ["Still"], "o": "However introduces a contrast: after the good news, a warning."}, {"a": 187, "b": 187, "l": "kt", "alt": ["helpful", "clear"], "o": "Reliable = you can trust it to be right every time."}, {"a": 194, "b": 194, "l": "kt", "alt": ["rough", "general"], "o": "Vague = not clear or not detailed. The opposite of precise."}, {"a": 201, "b": 201, "l": "kt", "alt": ["swapping"], "o": "Replacing A with B = putting B in the place of A."}, {"a": 205, "b": 205, "l": "tb", "alt": [], "o": "We say replace something WITH something else."}, {"a": 219, "b": 219, "l": "kt", "alt": ["likely"], "o": "Probably = likely, but not certain."}, {"a": 226, "b": 226, "l": "kt", "alt": ["on"], "o": "Read further = continue reading the next part."}, {"a": 236, "b": 236, "l": "pw", "alt": ["Lastly"], "o": "Finally introduces the last point of the article."}, {"a": 256, "b": 256, "l": "kt", "alt": ["notice", "see", "find"], "o": "To spot something = to notice or see it."}, {"a": 271, "b": 271, "l": "kt", "alt": ["cracks"], "o": "A detective solves a case = finds the answer to a mystery."}]}